WHAT IT CHANGES
  1. Act A's five figure titles become Sanaa's exact strings, with ONE
     deliberate exception recorded in a comment beside it (see BLOCKED below).
     The PENDING mechanism for the two unlanded renders is untouched, and the
     velocity figure keeps its stem `actA_velocity_field` while its title
     becomes her "Air speed, 305 W".
  2. `actA_monitor_replay`'s title loses the word "replayed", which is on her
     banned list.
  3. A PER-ACT solver line and scale line. These were not per-act before, and
     that mattered: Act A's line is FALSE for Act C. Measured in
     T25_MODULE_runs/T25_MOD_L1, constant/regionProperties reads `fluid ()`
     -- empty -- and `solid (module)`, and system/fvSchemes reads
     `divSchemes { default none; }`. Act C has ONE region, it is a solid, and
     no convective transport is solved: there is no k-omega SST, no turbulent
     forced convection and no conjugate coupling in that act. Act C's line is
     written from its own run.
  4. The replay-language purge across the narration, the provenance table,
     the solver.selected event and the report abstract: "recorded",
     "replayed", "screens come from that run", "no new number is produced",
     "the uploaded file is neither meshed nor solved", "Solver: none on this
     request" and the "Source case" path row are all gone. The provenance
     table's first two rows are now Solver and Scale, which say what the path
     was standing in for.
  5. CROSS-CASE TEXT REMOVED FROM ACT A (her item 5). The `agenda` list that
     feeds "Next investigations" was HARDCODED FOR BOTH ACTS, so Act A's
     screen carried the battery module's entry: "Resolve the coolant as a
     fluid region ... which is why no outlet temperature exists". That is
     battery text on a motor screen. The shared entry stays; the coolant
     entry moves to Act C's own `agenda_extra`.

WHAT IT DOES NOT CHANGE, AND WHY -- READ THIS BEFORE ASSUMING THE PASS IS DONE
  * Sanaa's third and fourth plain-fact sentences are NOT written, because
    NEITHER IS TRUE AS DRAFTED. Measured from the bundle:
      - "a planted 0.001 K perturbation": the planted magnitude is
        1.234e-03 K in all three Act A controls (PLANT = A24.PLANT, the frozen
        family constant, imported and never redefined). 0.001 K is a
        one-significant-figure rounding of it, not the value.
      - "agreement to 1e-5 K": the largest anchor residual is 3.7361e-05 K,
        3.7x that tolerance. The bundle's `abs_diff_degC: 0.0` is an artifact
        of check_anchors comparing `round(measured, 4)` against a hardcoded
        4-dp anchor table; the pre-registered gate in that function is
        `d <= 5e-5`, not 1e-5. "Agreement to better than 1e-4 K" is true.
    The instrument-check and anchor-check tables already print the real
    magnitudes and the real residuals, so omitting the two summary sentences
    removes nothing from the evidence and puts nothing false on screen.
  * `actA_map_table` KEEPS its existing title. Her string is "Peak core
    temperature, 16 operating points", but that figure plots the HOUSING peak
    -- every map_row's `source_field` ends .../housing/T -- and the bundle
    carries no core value. Her title becomes true when the core column lands.
  * The core peak column itself (her item 1) is NOT added here: it needs the
    bundle regenerated, which is the producer's job, not this module's.
  * Items 2 (rotor core -> core), 3 (drop the extrapolated headroom bars) and
    4 (0.1 C significant figures) are BUNDLE- AND PRODUCER-SIDE, not module-
    side, and are not in this patch. Item 6 belongs to the geometry lane.
    Item 7, the assumptions box, needs an artifact that does not exist.

RESTART SCOPE
  This patch is Python and NEEDS A SERVER RESTART to take effect. Bundle JSON
  and figure files are read inside `main()` at mission-run time (`_load_bundle`
  is called from the mission body, not at import), so every producer-side item
  above is DATA-ONLY and lands on the next mission run with no bounce. No HTML
  change is required by this patch.

